Or you can use MLM(R) for point estimates and fit and the bootstrap for confidence intervals. Typically, that's what you'd do with ML anyway. The bootstrap point estimates are only asymptotically equivalent to the computed point estimates from ML (any type, they're all the same), so with finite resamples you're better off with the ML estimates (assuming assumptions are met).

The purpose of the bootstrap--or MCMC CIs--is the confidence limits. As I've been saying, one choice does not lock you into the other.

