It is easier to simply set std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE than free first loadings and fix factor variances.  But in this case I think you should stick with the default method of fixing the first loading and freeing the factor variances.  It looks like the P=~f1 loading is trying its hardest to become orders of magnitude larger than its residual variance, which you have fixed to 1 (so it can't compensate by approaching zero).   In fact, before fitting a higher-order factor, just fit a CFA with the 3 lower-order factors.  With only 3 factors, that is statistically equivalent anyway, but you could take a look at the factor correlations and see whether a higher-order factor really fits the "observed" pattern.

